1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:04,137
My dear residents of Hadurok-ri.

2
00:00:04,204 --> 00:00:07,174
To stand before you here today

3
00:00:07,241 --> 00:00:08,575
and appoint our proud mascot,

4
00:00:08,642 --> 00:00:10,978
the Jeong-ipum-rok spotted deer Kkotdori,

5
00:00:11,044 --> 00:00:13,814
as the mascot to brighten the future
of Indi County,

6
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:16,984
is truly a great honor for me.

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,485
Now, as for our dear Kkotdori,

8
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:20,354
-as a deer of noble lineage,
-Hey!

9
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,555
a spotted deer that…

10
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:22,489
Joseon Dynasty…

11
00:00:22,556 --> 00:00:25,559
Lee Min-gi, you're so dead
when this is over.

12
00:00:25,626 --> 00:00:28,795
Okay, I'm sorry.

13
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:31,198
If you hit me, I'll take it.

14
00:00:31,265 --> 00:00:33,100
I'll do whatever you say.

15
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,769
Hey!

16
00:00:35,836 --> 00:00:37,137
Hold still.

17
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:41,308
Unanimously appointing Kkotdori
as Indi County's--

18
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,144
Hey, hold still! Hey!

19
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:50,284
Oh my!

20
00:00:54,621 --> 00:00:57,491
I walk down

21
00:00:57,558 --> 00:01:00,928
An endless road

22
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:06,166
When my heart looks for you

23
00:01:07,634 --> 00:01:10,871
The dazzling sunshine

24
00:01:10,938 --> 00:01:14,308
Brings you back to me

25
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:20,013
I get lost in memories

26
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:24,785
Where are you?

27
00:01:24,851 --> 00:01:28,188
Where are you, my love?

28
00:01:28,855 --> 00:01:32,492
Just like me

29
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:34,962
Are you crying too?

30
00:01:35,028 --> 00:01:38,999
Like the stars, like the moon

31
00:01:39,066 --> 00:01:42,502
Always in the same place

32
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:47,608
I'm always waiting only for you

33
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:53,246
Stay with me, County Governor!

34
00:01:53,313 --> 00:01:55,349
County Governor, wake up!

35
00:01:55,415 --> 00:01:58,652
County Governor, please wake up!
Are you okay, County Governor?

36
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:00,954
Careful with the County Governor.
Careful.

37
00:02:01,021 --> 00:02:02,656
Oh no, what do we do?

38
00:02:05,058 --> 00:02:07,294
-rammed him right in the chest.
-I know.

39
00:02:09,529 --> 00:02:10,998
What is the meaning of this?

40
00:02:11,565 --> 00:02:13,433
What on earth happened here?

41
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:16,803
I'm so sorry.
He's normally so gentle…

42
00:02:17,738 --> 00:02:19,206
This makes no sense…

43
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,712
Wait, is that really our Kkotdori?

44
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:28,682
He looks a bit different.

45
00:02:28,749 --> 00:02:30,317
What?

46
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,553
You're right.

47
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:36,390
There's no scar on his leg,
and his antlers are different.

48
00:02:36,456 --> 00:02:38,592
So you're saying this one's a fake?

49
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:42,029
Hey, Village Head, you explain this!

50
00:02:42,095 --> 00:02:43,830
What's going on here?

51
00:02:45,399 --> 00:02:47,067
Um, well, you see…

52
00:02:47,134 --> 00:02:49,936
Why can't you say anything? Kkotdori!

53
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:51,071
Where's our Kkotdori?

54
00:02:51,138 --> 00:02:52,873
Where is our Kkotdori?

55
00:02:52,939 --> 00:02:54,374
Um, well, the thing is…

56
00:02:54,441 --> 00:02:55,776
Please, stop.

57
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:00,547
I'll tell you everything honestly.

58
00:03:02,449 --> 00:03:05,218
Fine, you explain it.

59
00:03:05,285 --> 00:03:07,454
Where is our Kkotdori?

60
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:16,329
Kkotdori…

61
00:03:17,931 --> 00:03:18,799
is dead.

62
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,400
-What?

63
00:03:21,134 --> 00:03:22,202
Why?

64
00:03:24,404 --> 00:03:25,972
He was hit by a tractor.

65
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,641
A tractor--

66
00:03:28,141 --> 00:03:29,376
Who did it?

67
00:03:29,443 --> 00:03:31,211
Who on earth did it!

68
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:49,629
Yun-hui did it.

69
00:03:49,696 --> 00:03:51,431
Yun-hui did it.

70
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:55,001
I'm sorry, Yun-hui.

71
00:03:56,002 --> 00:03:57,904
You'll just get yelled at,

72
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:00,240
but if I'm kicked out, my life is over.

73
00:04:00,307 --> 00:04:02,909
I'm sorry, Yun-hui. Truly sorry.

74
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:09,816
Yun-hui!

75
00:04:11,017 --> 00:04:13,587
The mascot appointment
is hereby canceled.

76
00:04:13,653 --> 00:04:16,189
Excuse me, what about the prize money…

77
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,457
Canceled, obviously.

78
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:22,295
I will report every detail of this
to the County Governor.

79
00:04:22,362 --> 00:04:25,565
We won't let this slide,
so brace yourselves.

80
00:04:25,632 --> 00:04:27,367
Um, Miss…

81
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:32,572
Wait, at least meet my son,
the Head of the Youth Association…

82
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:59,332
I'm really sorry, okay?

83
00:04:59,399 --> 00:05:03,036
I'll definitely pay you back
for this favor!

84
00:05:13,013 --> 00:05:15,615
Hey, you son of a b**ch!

85
00:05:29,095 --> 00:05:32,199
I'm sorry…

86
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:42,509
-Hey!
-Min-gi, hey!

87
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,516
WELCOME, JEONG-IPUM-ROK KKOTDORI

88
00:05:57,157 --> 00:06:00,427
This is an utterly unforgivable
incident!

89
00:06:00,493 --> 00:06:01,928
These punks…

90
00:06:01,995 --> 00:06:05,265
killed our village's sacred Kkotdori,

91
00:06:05,332 --> 00:06:09,202
made fools of us all
with a fake Kkotdori,

92
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:12,372
and even gored a hole
in the County Governor's belly,

93
00:06:12,439 --> 00:06:15,141
committing an unforgivable crime!

94
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,811
Because of them, our long-awaited…

95
00:06:18,478 --> 00:06:21,448
road-paving project went up in smoke!

96
00:06:22,616 --> 00:06:23,583
On top of that…

97
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:26,186
stealing apples, trashing flower beds,

98
00:06:26,253 --> 00:06:29,356
peeing in the reservoir, and so on!

99
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:33,059
Too many crimes to even list…

100
00:06:33,126 --> 00:06:37,197
They're the worst menaces
to ever disturb our village!

101
00:06:37,264 --> 00:06:40,834
Therefore, I hereby propose…

102
00:06:40,901 --> 00:06:43,670
that these devils be banished at once!

103
00:06:46,273 --> 00:06:48,508
Shouldn't we get a chance to speak too?

104
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:52,012
Look here, he says
he still has something to say.

105
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:54,014
Fine, go ahead and try.

106
00:06:57,050 --> 00:06:59,352
HOME OF JEONG-IPUM-ROK
LIVELY HADUROK-RI

107
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:03,924
You seem to be viewing this case
far too emotionally…

108
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:06,459
Let's think about this calmly.

109
00:07:06,526 --> 00:07:09,362
Yes, it is true.

110
00:07:09,429 --> 00:07:13,667
I hit Kkotdori with the tractor.

111
00:07:14,534 --> 00:07:18,271
However, if that deer named Kkotdori
or whatever

112
00:07:18,338 --> 00:07:20,240
had been properly locked in its pen,

113
00:07:20,307 --> 00:07:22,909
this terrible tractor accident

114
00:07:22,976 --> 00:07:24,911
never would have happened at all.

115
00:07:24,978 --> 00:07:28,748
In other words, the biggest cause
of this incident…

116
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:32,652
is that you failed to manage
Kkotdori properly!

117
00:07:32,719 --> 00:07:35,021
Isn't that right, everyone?

118
00:07:35,088 --> 00:07:36,823
What kind of--

119
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:39,392
Everyone, right now this punk…

120
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:42,095
is spouting complete nonsense!

121
00:07:44,864 --> 00:07:46,466
Nonsense, you say?

122
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,235
Very well.

123
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:52,472
Then let me give you an example.

124
00:07:52,539 --> 00:07:55,608
Even now, on highways across the nation,

125
00:07:55,675 --> 00:07:58,244
countless wild animals…

126
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,547
are hit by cars and die every single day.

127
00:08:00,613 --> 00:08:03,049
If so…

128
00:08:03,116 --> 00:08:07,053
are those drivers criminals too?

129
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:12,092
Should those drivers be banished
from this country too?

130
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,860
That would be unfair.

131
00:08:13,927 --> 00:08:17,764
Now that I hear it,
it's weirdly convincing.

132
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:21,234
So this incident
was just an unavoidable accident…

133
00:08:21,301 --> 00:08:23,903
and not entirely our fault,

134
00:08:23,970 --> 00:08:26,206
as I strongly contend!

135
00:08:26,272 --> 00:08:29,743
Done yapping?
All right, let's put it to a vote.

136
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:34,748
All in favor of banishing these punks,
raise your hand.

137
00:08:39,052 --> 00:08:40,353
Aren't you raising yours?

138
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:47,527
All right, by an overwhelming majority…

139
00:08:48,928 --> 00:08:51,064
you guys are banished!

140
00:08:51,131 --> 00:08:52,632
That's completely unfair!

141
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:56,403
Unfair, my foot! Cut the crap,
pack your bags, and get out now!

142
00:08:56,469 --> 00:08:59,272
I'm just trying to farm on my own land.

143
00:08:59,339 --> 00:09:01,674
What right do you have to kick me out?

144
00:09:01,741 --> 00:09:04,010
We don't accept this,

145
00:09:04,077 --> 00:09:05,845
so let's do this by the law.

146
00:09:05,912 --> 00:09:09,849
File a complaint
and let's have a proper trial.

147
00:09:09,916 --> 00:09:11,718
Hey, let's go.

148
00:09:11,785 --> 00:09:13,486
That little punk.

149
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:15,989
The law, my…

150
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:18,324
Kids today have no respect.

151
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,926
My, people from Seoul sure…

152
00:09:19,993 --> 00:09:22,595
Those fearless little punks.

153
00:09:22,662 --> 00:09:26,132
Fine. We'll see whether
you punks leave or not.

154
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:32,505
Now then,
next is our current Village Head.

155
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:35,542
We will now move on to the meeting
regarding Kang Yun-hui.

156
00:09:35,608 --> 00:09:36,643
What's that mean?

157
00:09:36,709 --> 00:09:38,278
Why bring Yun-hui into this?

158
00:09:38,344 --> 00:09:40,313
Those punks framed her, remember?

159
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,515
Either way, Yun-hui conspired
with those punks

160
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,484
and tried to fool all of us!

161
00:09:44,551 --> 00:09:46,052
Yun-hui's an accomplice too!

162
00:09:46,119 --> 00:09:48,788
Yun-hui, step down as Village Head.

163
00:09:48,855 --> 00:09:50,890
We can't trust you with it anymore.

164
00:09:50,957 --> 00:09:53,159
Isn't that right, everyone?

165
00:09:53,226 --> 00:09:55,728
-That's not right.
-Isn't that too harsh?

166
00:09:55,795 --> 00:09:57,831
Right, that's right.

167
00:09:59,899 --> 00:10:03,203
Even if we say Yun-hui is partly to blame,

168
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:06,973
this still isn't a reason for her
to step down as Village Head.

169
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,808
Actually, now that it's come up,

170
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:13,413
Yun-hui took on all the village dirty work
and worked herself to the bone.

171
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,914
Isn't that right?

172
00:10:14,981 --> 00:10:16,716
If anyone here farmed without

173
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:18,818
Yun-hui's help, step forward!

174
00:10:18,885 --> 00:10:21,754
We all know that already…

175
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:25,625
Plus, don't you know the Township
Athletic Meet is coming up soon?

176
00:10:25,692 --> 00:10:28,528
Yun-hui has prepared so well until now.

177
00:10:28,595 --> 00:10:32,932
If we replace her now,
we'll lose again! Again!

178
00:10:32,999 --> 00:10:36,269
We'll lose to those damn
Sangdurok-ri jerks again!

179
00:10:39,038 --> 00:10:40,340
Have you all forgotten

180
00:10:40,406 --> 00:10:43,610
those humiliating defeats
over the past nine years?

181
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:48,381
If y'all want to lose again this year,

182
00:10:48,448 --> 00:10:51,251
go ahead and replace the Village Head
as you please.

183
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,386
Does the meet matter right now?

184
00:10:53,453 --> 00:10:56,556
Our Kkotdori is dead! Kkotdori!

185
00:10:56,623 --> 00:11:00,493
Since when did you care so much about
Kkotdori to throw a fit like this?

186
00:11:01,394 --> 00:11:04,697
And speaking frankly,
is that even Kkotdori?

187
00:11:05,431 --> 00:11:09,102
The Jeong-ipum-rok line died out ages ago,
yet you still harp on Kkotdori.

188
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:12,172
We swapped in a fake Kkotdori
to save the village's face.

189
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:13,706
Does anyone here not know?

190
00:11:16,943 --> 00:11:20,580
You punk! What if someone
from another village hears you?

191
00:11:20,647 --> 00:11:23,249
Then why make a big deal out of nothing

192
00:11:23,316 --> 00:11:26,186
and drag Yun-hui into it, you bastard?

193
00:11:26,252 --> 00:11:29,155
You just want to be
Village Head again, you punk,

194
00:11:29,222 --> 00:11:31,291
spouting all this nonsense, you bastard.

195
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,560
When did I? When did I, you punk!

196
00:11:33,626 --> 00:11:34,861
Knock it off, both of you.

197
00:11:38,231 --> 00:11:40,667
Then how about we do this?

198
00:11:41,434 --> 00:11:44,971
If Yun-hui wins the Township Athletic Meet

199
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:47,707
and brings back the trophy
after ten years,

200
00:11:47,774 --> 00:11:49,943
she stays on as Village Head.

201
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:54,214
If she doesn't win, she steps down.
How's that?

202
00:11:55,782 --> 00:11:57,050
Grandpa, that's a bit…

203
00:11:57,116 --> 00:12:01,221
If you're not confident, give up
the Village Head post right now.

204
00:12:09,696 --> 00:12:10,830
This drives me crazy.

205
00:12:13,199 --> 00:12:15,001
Kang Yun-hui, that nasty brat.

206
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:17,704
I took a punch to the jaw for her,
so she should've taken the fall!

207
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:19,606
She spilled the beans already?

208
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:24,077
I think my jaw is cracked.

209
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,246
Look, a news article's out!

210
00:12:26,312 --> 00:12:29,816
"Indi County Governor Gored in Belly
by Deer Antlers at Event,"

211
00:12:29,882 --> 00:12:31,951
"Rushed to Hospital in Freak Accident."

212
00:12:32,619 --> 00:12:35,755
Wait, deer antlers can actually
pierce a person's belly.

213
00:12:35,822 --> 00:12:38,091
Right, that Jeong-ipum-rok or whatever…

214
00:12:38,157 --> 00:12:40,026
Maybe it really did
beat up barbarians.

215
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:41,561
Right, I know.

216
00:12:41,628 --> 00:12:43,529
It really could be true.

217
00:12:45,198 --> 00:12:48,468
By the way, you got a little tanned.

218
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:50,703
I told you to wear sunscreen, dude.

219
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,005
Forget it.

220
00:12:52,071 --> 00:12:54,040
Sunscreen is too weak for a real man.

221
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:55,041
Right, Han-cheol…

222
00:12:58,244 --> 00:13:00,213
Where did Han-cheol go? Han-cheol!

223
00:13:03,583 --> 00:13:05,118
Where did he go?

224
00:13:06,085 --> 00:13:07,220
What?

225
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:10,089
Farm cabbages to put out an album?

226
00:13:10,156 --> 00:13:11,958
I was out of my mind, totally crazy.

227
00:13:12,025 --> 00:13:13,693
I'll just quit everything,

228
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,362
go to Seoul, have one passionate
romance, and die.

229
00:13:16,429 --> 00:13:17,930
Jeez, seriously!

230
00:13:24,437 --> 00:13:26,005
Gosh, really.

231
00:13:35,882 --> 00:13:39,886
VILLAGE BUS, INDI

232
00:14:05,311 --> 00:14:08,348
Excuse me, is this Hadurok-ri?

233
00:14:10,316 --> 00:14:12,151
Thank you.

234
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:20,193
Hey, aren't you getting on?

235
00:14:20,259 --> 00:14:23,930
What? Oh, I'm getting on.

236
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:25,998
-Han-cheol!

237
00:14:26,065 --> 00:14:28,601
-Hey!
-Seriously!

238
00:14:29,235 --> 00:14:31,904
-Han-cheol!

239
00:14:33,506 --> 00:14:36,008
If he was gone,
you should've told me earlier!

240
00:14:36,075 --> 00:14:38,444
How was I supposed to know
he packed and left, man?

241
00:14:38,511 --> 00:14:40,480
That disloyal bastard, seriously!

242
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:43,950
Jeez, he must've left already!
This is driving me crazy.

243
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:50,923
Huh? Han-cheol! Han-cheol!

244
00:14:52,925 --> 00:14:54,861
Han-cheol, you haven't left yet.

245
00:14:54,927 --> 00:14:57,497
Hey, I'm sorry.
Let's talk it out, okay?

246
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,065
Man, no matter how mad you are,

247
00:14:59,132 --> 00:15:01,033
how can you leave without a word?

248
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:04,804
Guys, let me ask you one thing.

249
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:08,841
Huh? Sure, ask away. Ask anything.

250
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:12,645
When you see someone
for the first time in your life…

251
00:15:12,712 --> 00:15:14,781
and your heart…

252
00:15:14,847 --> 00:15:17,850
pounds like it'll break your ribs,
why is that…

253
00:15:18,885 --> 00:15:21,320
-I wonder?
-What?

254
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:24,390
We only brushed past each other,

255
00:15:25,124 --> 00:15:28,127
yet my mind goes hazy,

256
00:15:28,194 --> 00:15:31,097
and whether my eyes are open or shut,

257
00:15:31,164 --> 00:15:33,933
I keep thinking of that person.

258
00:15:35,334 --> 00:15:36,335
Why is that?

259
00:15:36,402 --> 00:15:38,871
From an expert's perspective,

260
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:43,009
this seems like a classic symptom
of a man in love.

261
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:47,547
I knew it. So that's what it was.

262
00:15:48,815 --> 00:15:50,483
Guys…

263
00:15:51,350 --> 00:15:53,286
I think I…

264
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,123
just fell in love.

265
00:16:01,194 --> 00:16:02,628
With who in this country?

266
00:16:28,754 --> 00:16:30,923
This is driving me crazy, really.

267
00:16:31,691 --> 00:16:34,260
It's all because of that jerk
Lee Min-gi, jeez.

268
00:16:35,027 --> 00:16:37,230
Those rotten jerks.

269
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:38,631
He won't get away with it!

270
00:16:38,698 --> 00:16:39,932
Gosh, forget it.

271
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,968
They're not worth it. Sit down.

272
00:16:42,034 --> 00:16:42,935
Sit down.

273
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,637
Anyway,

274
00:16:44,704 --> 00:16:47,740
Man-gu looked dead set on it.

275
00:16:47,807 --> 00:16:50,910
He's already campaigning
for the next Village Head election.

276
00:16:50,977 --> 00:16:53,045
He's obsessed with titles, isn't he?

277
00:16:53,112 --> 00:16:56,782
Still, even if it's a losing battle,
I'm going to give it a shot.

278
00:16:56,849 --> 00:16:59,919
Sang-deuk, we're starting real practice
tomorrow,

279
00:16:59,986 --> 00:17:01,487
so gather the Youth Association

280
00:17:01,554 --> 00:17:03,689
at the branch school field
after work, okay?

281
00:17:03,756 --> 00:17:05,625
Right, got it.

282
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:08,060
Ever since those punks moved here,

283
00:17:08,127 --> 00:17:10,930
there hasn't been a single quiet day.
Not a single one.

284
00:17:11,764 --> 00:17:15,468
Didn't you say those guys
were in a band in Seoul?

285
00:17:16,502 --> 00:17:18,204
I heard they're handsome too.

286
00:17:18,271 --> 00:17:19,472
Why do you care?

287
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:21,407
Wait, are you into those jerks?

288
00:17:21,474 --> 00:17:24,577
What? Rather than being into them,

289
00:17:24,644 --> 00:17:27,146
as a future professional
in the same industry,

290
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,881
call it camaraderie?

291
00:17:28,948 --> 00:17:31,183
Later, when I become an idol,

292
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:33,719
we might even meet on stage, you know.

293
00:17:38,691 --> 00:17:41,327
No! I'm going to be an idol!

294
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:43,229
-A sexy girl group!
-Stop her, quick.

295
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:48,768
Just you dare cut my hair!

296
00:17:48,834 --> 00:17:50,803
Then jeez, I'll really di--

297
00:17:52,004 --> 00:17:52,872
I'll run away!

298
00:17:57,543 --> 00:17:59,178
No matter how mad you are,

299
00:18:00,146 --> 00:18:01,881
how can you curse at your kid?

300
00:18:01,948 --> 00:18:04,216
Wait, was that a curse just now?

301
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:06,852
It all looks the same to the rest of us.

302
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:10,323
How on earth do you understand
all that so well, huh?

303
00:18:10,389 --> 00:18:12,959
It's all in the details. The details.

304
00:18:13,025 --> 00:18:15,595
The angle of his knuckles differs,

305
00:18:15,661 --> 00:18:17,663
and his vocal tone subtly shifts.

306
00:18:17,730 --> 00:18:20,399
That never stops amazing me.

307
00:18:20,466 --> 00:18:22,301
Huh? Who's that?

308
00:18:22,368 --> 00:18:24,136
Excuse me.

309
00:18:24,203 --> 00:18:26,238
Um, is this the Village Head's house?

310
00:18:26,305 --> 00:18:29,875
Yes, I'm the Village Head.
What can I do for you?

311
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:33,079
Hello! I'm a college volunteer
from Seoul who paints murals.

312
00:18:33,145 --> 00:18:34,680
Mural volunteering?

313
00:18:34,747 --> 00:18:37,116
Yes, on plain country village walls,

314
00:18:37,183 --> 00:18:40,519
I paint flowers, butterflies,
and other pretty pictures for you.

315
00:18:42,188 --> 00:18:43,856
Yes, and?

316
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:47,793
I was hoping to paint some pictures
on the walls of this village.

317
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:50,463
Oh, really?

318
00:18:52,365 --> 00:18:55,234
What's wrong? Would you rather I didn't?

319
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:58,638
Well, it's not really something
we need around here.

320
00:18:59,271 --> 00:19:03,643
Honestly, having an outsider around
just stirs up the whole village.

321
00:19:03,709 --> 00:19:07,079
And frankly, we don't even know
where you're from or what you do…

322
00:19:08,347 --> 00:19:10,916
I'm not a shady person.
Please don't worry about that.

323
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:15,121
Like a shady person would ever say,
"Hey, I'm shady"?

324
00:19:15,187 --> 00:19:17,623
Why our village, of all places?

325
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:19,392
Just go try another village.

326
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,961
Well, um, I…

327
00:19:22,028 --> 00:19:23,929
I just fell in love with this village!

328
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:26,265
And if I paint murals,
tourists will come visit,

329
00:19:26,332 --> 00:19:27,900
which would help the village…

330
00:19:27,967 --> 00:19:32,038
Come on, all tourists ever do
is leave a bunch of trash behind.

331
00:19:32,104 --> 00:19:33,873
It just messes up the village.

332
00:19:33,939 --> 00:19:37,543
Um, it's also good for
children's emotional development.

333
00:19:37,610 --> 00:19:40,880
Emotional development, my ass!
We're too busy trying to get by.

334
00:19:40,946 --> 00:19:43,616
Forget it and go try another village.

335
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:45,785
I really have my heart set on this.

336
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:48,587
Could you please let me
volunteer here?

337
00:19:48,654 --> 00:19:52,158
I'll stay quiet as a mouse, paint,
and vanish like I was never here, okay?

338
00:19:52,224 --> 00:19:54,160
Do you really want to do it that badly?

339
00:19:54,226 --> 00:19:56,862
Yes, please let me do it.

340
00:19:56,929 --> 00:20:00,466
But that's going to take
more than a day or two.

341
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:02,034
What about food and lodging?

342
00:20:02,101 --> 00:20:04,503
I guess I'll get a room
at an inn in town.

343
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:06,338
Um, by any chance, are you married?

344
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:10,009
No, I'm only 23.

345
00:20:10,076 --> 00:20:11,243
Really?

346
00:20:11,310 --> 00:20:14,280
We have plenty of spare rooms.
Shall I give you one?

347
00:20:15,648 --> 00:20:18,150
No, I wouldn't want to impose on you.

348
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:19,919
Oh, goodness, it's no trouble!

349
00:20:19,985 --> 00:20:22,354
We have the room, and I'll just set
one extra place at the table.

350
00:20:22,421 --> 00:20:25,825
Well, since you insist,
I'll gladly accept.

351
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,860
-Thank you.
-Hey, Sang-deuk!

352
00:20:27,927 --> 00:20:30,563
Hurry and show the young lady
to the guest room.

353
00:20:30,629 --> 00:20:34,133
This is my son, and he's still single.
A bachelor!

354
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:37,236
He's handsome, has a great personality,

355
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:38,771
and he's strong!

356
00:20:38,838 --> 00:20:42,475
Mom, there you go again.

357
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:46,045
What are you doing? She's young enough
to be my niece!

358
00:20:46,112 --> 00:20:48,180
Quiet! Hurry and show her to her room.

359
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:50,916
Go on, you two.
Have a nice chat,

360
00:20:50,983 --> 00:20:52,585
and grab a cup of coffee.

361
00:21:00,192 --> 00:21:03,095
How is it? Do you like the room?

362
00:21:03,162 --> 00:21:06,132
Yes, it's nice and cozy.
Thank you.

363
00:21:06,198 --> 00:21:09,068
And don't mind what my mom said.

364
00:21:09,135 --> 00:21:11,504
Seeing me get married
is her lifelong wish,

365
00:21:11,570 --> 00:21:13,606
so she'll probably bug you a lot.

366
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:17,009
-Okay.
-Don't worry, though.

367
00:21:17,743 --> 00:21:19,445
You're not my type anyway.

368
00:21:20,312 --> 00:21:22,815
I like sexy women.

369
00:21:23,749 --> 00:21:26,852
You know, voluptuous? Right?

370
00:21:31,157 --> 00:21:35,494
So you were about to ditch everything
and take off,

371
00:21:35,561 --> 00:21:39,431
but you saw some woman get off a bus
and fell in love at first sight.

372
00:21:42,101 --> 00:21:44,103
And you don't know who she is,

373
00:21:44,170 --> 00:21:46,272
or even where she lives.

374
00:21:48,541 --> 00:21:49,809
Tell me, though…

375
00:21:51,744 --> 00:21:53,245
-Is she pretty?

376
00:21:58,484 --> 00:22:00,252
How's her body?

377
00:22:03,923 --> 00:22:06,926
Man, just how amazing is this woman

378
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:09,195
to have this block of wood
acting like that?

379
00:22:09,261 --> 00:22:12,164
At least we don't have to worry
about him running away now.

380
00:22:17,503 --> 00:22:19,605
Why is the day so long?

381
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:22,474
We've got more shoveling tomorrow.
Let's get to sleep.

382
00:22:28,781 --> 00:22:29,915
Darn, it's so hot.

383
00:22:29,982 --> 00:22:32,551
Can't we crack the door open
while we sleep?

384
00:22:32,618 --> 00:22:33,786
Are you crazy?

385
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:36,121
This room is already
half air, half mosquitoes.

386
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,489
Sleep with the door open?

387
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:39,425
If you're unlucky, you'll bleed out—

388
00:22:39,491 --> 00:22:41,827
bitten to death right here
by mosquitoes, punk!

389
00:22:41,894 --> 00:22:44,864
Come on, what kind of real man
makes a fuss over something so small?

390
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:46,899
Bites from mosquitoes like these
barely even show.

391
00:22:46,966 --> 00:22:49,001
Shut up and turn off the light.

392
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:50,402
Turn it off.

393
00:22:50,469 --> 00:22:53,272
Jeez, I can't sleep when it's hot.

394
00:22:54,273 --> 00:22:56,942
Looks like I'll be up all night
because of you guys.

395
00:22:58,010 --> 00:23:01,180
I'm exhausted,
and I can't even get any sleep…

396
00:23:13,359 --> 00:23:16,896
Hey, quit squirming around.

397
00:23:16,962 --> 00:23:18,964
I'm a light sleeper.

398
00:23:19,031 --> 00:23:22,768
Sorry. Go to sleep, go to sleep.

399
00:23:28,007 --> 00:23:30,542
TOWN BUS, IN-DI

400
00:23:42,054 --> 00:23:45,391
Hey, what's that thumping sound?

401
00:23:45,457 --> 00:23:46,926
Han-cheol, is that you?

402
00:23:46,992 --> 00:23:52,431
Thinking about that woman again, huh?
Let me get some sleep.

403
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,635
You can hear this?

404
00:23:56,702 --> 00:23:58,671
Told you I'm a light sleeper.

405
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:03,075
Don't curse at me…

406
00:24:10,382 --> 00:24:11,417
SOUL-MYEON

407
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:12,851
HADUROK-RI

408
00:24:42,281 --> 00:24:43,615
Ugh, this punk…

409
00:24:43,682 --> 00:24:45,718
What did you eat, you bastard?

410
00:24:52,358 --> 00:24:55,627
Two o'clock! Man, we overslept again!

411
00:24:56,295 --> 00:24:58,597
Hey, wake up! Wake up!

412
00:25:00,366 --> 00:25:02,801
Hey! Wake up!

413
00:25:04,136 --> 00:25:05,371
Where'd Ki-jun go?

414
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:06,438
Ki-jun!

415
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:10,743
Gosh, after complaining so much
about the heat last night,

416
00:25:10,809 --> 00:25:12,644
he went outside after all.

417
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:14,480
Hey, Ki-jun, wake up.

418
00:25:14,546 --> 00:25:16,348
Hey, wake up… Huh?

419
00:25:18,917 --> 00:25:20,652
Whoa! What do we do?

420
00:25:20,719 --> 00:25:21,887
Hey, wake up!

421
00:25:21,954 --> 00:25:23,122
Man, you look crazy!

422
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,324
Why is it so loud out here?

423
00:25:30,062 --> 00:25:32,664
Man, keep it down…

424
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:44,343
My face… What happened to my face?

425
00:25:44,410 --> 00:25:45,978
Man, on a scorching day like this,

426
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:48,280
you left your face out in the sun
for hours.

427
00:25:48,347 --> 00:25:49,715
How could it not burn?

428
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,885
Man, you're nicely roasted.

429
00:25:53,752 --> 00:25:56,688
My, oh my, after going on and on
about being a real man,

430
00:25:56,755 --> 00:25:59,058
you donated plenty of blood
to the mosquitoes, sir!

431
00:25:59,124 --> 00:26:01,193
Are you guys messing with me?

432
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,195
My face…

433
00:26:03,962 --> 00:26:05,964
What is this, seriously?

434
00:26:06,031 --> 00:26:09,768
Why? It's dark and bumpy.
Total real-man material.

435
00:26:09,835 --> 00:26:13,405
Plus, it's exotic.
Southeast Asian alpha-male style.

436
00:26:13,472 --> 00:26:15,674
Knock it off already!

437
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,509
All right, punk.

438
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:20,946
I'll go into town later
and buy you some ointment, so don't worry.

439
00:26:21,013 --> 00:26:22,948
-Into town?
-Yes.

440
00:26:23,015 --> 00:26:24,750
We need to buy rice,

441
00:26:24,817 --> 00:26:27,319
and the field's almost plowed,
so we need cabbage seeds too.

442
00:26:27,386 --> 00:26:29,955
Then while we're there,
let's buy some meat too.

443
00:26:30,022 --> 00:26:31,557
I want meat! Meat, meat!

444
00:26:31,623 --> 00:26:32,958
All right, punk.

445
00:26:33,025 --> 00:26:35,894
Today, I'll treat you to
white rice and beef soup.

446
00:26:35,961 --> 00:26:37,629
You mean it?

447
00:26:42,835 --> 00:26:44,503
What's that sound?

448
00:26:45,804 --> 00:26:46,972
No way…

449
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,918
What are you doing, ma'am?

450
00:26:59,985 --> 00:27:02,821
We don't have any side dishes for dinner,
so I'm making some.

451
00:27:02,888 --> 00:27:05,157
Are you heading out to paint?

452
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:09,628
No, I'm going to look around town
and brainstorm first today.

453
00:27:09,695 --> 00:27:10,762
Is that so?

454
00:27:10,829 --> 00:27:12,998
Then you can go around
with my son, Sang-deuk.

455
00:27:14,233 --> 00:27:19,037
No, I focus much better
when I brainstorm my art alone.

456
00:27:19,838 --> 00:27:23,008
Instead, could I borrow that bicycle?

457
00:27:23,075 --> 00:27:25,544
Sure, go ahead.

458
00:27:25,611 --> 00:27:27,012
Thank you.

459
00:27:31,550 --> 00:27:33,185
I'll be back.

460
00:27:38,090 --> 00:27:42,694
My goodness, she's so pretty
and so polite.

461
00:27:43,996 --> 00:27:46,565
She'd be the perfect
daughter-in-law for me.

462
00:27:47,933 --> 00:27:50,502
Please help me, Father.

463
00:27:50,569 --> 00:27:52,671
Huh? Why?

464
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:57,442
Not you, Father.

465
00:28:12,858 --> 00:28:14,145
SOUL-MYEON

466
00:28:15,794 --> 00:28:17,129
HADUROK-RI

467
00:28:20,599 --> 00:28:21,900
HADUROK-RI

468
00:28:26,438 --> 00:28:28,640
Disrespectful punks.

469
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:37,316
Mister, what are you doing
in front of our house?

470
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:41,286
Can't you tell?
I'm cutting off your electricity.

471
00:28:41,353 --> 00:28:43,589
What? Why are you cutting
our electricity?

472
00:28:43,655 --> 00:28:45,557
Power lines don't reach
out here, you know.

473
00:28:45,624 --> 00:28:46,825
So when your grandma was alive,

474
00:28:46,892 --> 00:28:48,961
she drew electricity from my house.

475
00:28:49,027 --> 00:28:51,930
Now that she's gone,
I'm cleaning it up.

476
00:28:51,997 --> 00:28:53,599
Why? Got a problem with that?

477
00:28:53,665 --> 00:28:55,234
If you do, sue me.

478
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:56,501
You guys love the law.

479
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:58,537
How are we supposed to live
if you cut that?

480
00:28:58,604 --> 00:29:01,073
Beats me. How will you live
without electricity?

481
00:29:01,139 --> 00:29:03,675
If you can't take it, then leave.

482
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,344
Forget it, whatever.

483
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:07,779
Did people in the Joseon Dynasty
need electricity to live?

484
00:29:07,846 --> 00:29:10,282
We'll live by candlelight. Candlelight!

485
00:29:10,349 --> 00:29:11,783
Saves on the bill, anyway.

486
00:29:11,850 --> 00:29:13,752
You'll save on water, too.

487
00:29:13,819 --> 00:29:15,254
Your water's getting cut.

488
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:17,356
Your water came from my house, too.

489
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:21,426
Boy, saving on water too?
You're going to be so rich.

490
00:29:23,895 --> 00:29:24,963
I'm so pissed!

491
00:29:26,231 --> 00:29:27,733
What's his deal?

492
00:29:36,241 --> 00:29:38,343
Darn it, what's wrong with this thing?

493
00:29:39,811 --> 00:29:41,913
I didn't do that.

494
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:45,450
Come on, let's just go!

495
00:29:45,517 --> 00:29:48,186
Seriously, it's one thing
after another.

496
00:29:52,057 --> 00:29:55,093
Looks like they're dead set
on driving us out.

497
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:57,029
Fine, let's see who wins.

498
00:29:58,130 --> 00:30:00,732
Stop scratching!
You're making me itch, too.

499
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,501
It itches like crazy, though!

500
00:30:02,567 --> 00:30:04,403
Look at this! It itches to death.

501
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:09,107
A snake! Snake! Snake!

502
00:30:10,142 --> 00:30:13,845
What is this place, a safari?
The Serengeti?

503
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:17,516
Deer, snakes, mosquitoes.
What a colorful variety!

504
00:30:17,582 --> 00:30:18,684
It's coming this way!

505
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:21,520
-It's coming this way! Right here!
-Hey, hey, hey!

506
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,655
What? What is that?

507
00:30:25,957 --> 00:30:27,626
What's wrong with you?

508
00:30:27,693 --> 00:30:30,195
-What's your deal?
-Stop it! Get that away!

509
00:30:34,666 --> 00:30:37,336
Ma'am! Ma'am, ma'am…

510
00:30:38,236 --> 00:30:39,404
What's with you guys?

511
00:30:39,471 --> 00:30:41,506
My son told me not to even talk to you.

512
00:30:41,573 --> 00:30:42,441
Go away! Shoo!

513
00:30:42,507 --> 00:30:45,243
You don't have to talk to us, just do
something about this crazy woman!

514
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:47,245
-Crazy woman?
-Her!

515
00:30:47,846 --> 00:30:49,481
Oh, Song Hwa-ran.

516
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:55,020
-Do you know her?
-She works at my place.

517
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:57,689
Song Hwa-ran, what's wrong?
What is it?

518
00:30:59,057 --> 00:31:02,327
Oh, you want them to give you
that snake?

519
00:31:02,394 --> 00:31:05,430
What? So she chased us
just to ask for that snake?

520
00:31:05,497 --> 00:31:09,000
Why didn't you say so
instead of scaring us like that?

521
00:31:09,067 --> 00:31:10,769
She doesn't talk much.

522
00:31:10,836 --> 00:31:13,939
We're not the snake's guardians.
Why ask us?

523
00:31:14,005 --> 00:31:15,841
Just take it and go!

524
00:31:17,976 --> 00:31:18,977
They said take it.

525
00:31:22,381 --> 00:31:25,117
-What is that?
-Are those all snakes?

526
00:31:25,183 --> 00:31:26,418
They're snakes.

527
00:31:32,958 --> 00:31:35,193
Whoa! She caught another one!

528
00:31:35,260 --> 00:31:36,895
She's a total snake catcher.

529
00:31:36,962 --> 00:31:39,331
You're having a lucky day,
Song Hwa-ran.

530
00:31:39,398 --> 00:31:41,933
What's a young woman doing
something like that for?

531
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:44,102
Don't say that. Poor thing.

532
00:31:44,169 --> 00:31:45,771
Poor thing? Why?

533
00:31:45,837 --> 00:31:47,472
Well…

534
00:31:48,373 --> 00:31:51,810
This is strictly between us,
so don't breathe a word to anyone.

535
00:31:52,310 --> 00:31:53,779
Song Hwa-ran…

536
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:56,982
She's an illegal immigrant.

537
00:31:57,048 --> 00:31:58,550
She came from Yanbian to make money,

538
00:31:58,617 --> 00:32:01,086
got kicked out of her factory
without getting paid,

539
00:32:01,153 --> 00:32:03,955
and I felt so bad for her
that I hired her.

540
00:32:04,022 --> 00:32:05,390
Why is she catching snakes, though?

541
00:32:05,457 --> 00:32:06,324
A side job.

542
00:32:06,391 --> 00:32:09,428
Selling them to a snake soup place
pays pretty well.

543
00:32:10,195 --> 00:32:12,364
To feed her family back in Yanbian,

544
00:32:12,431 --> 00:32:14,266
she does anything that makes money.

545
00:32:14,332 --> 00:32:15,734
Catches snakes, digs up roots,

546
00:32:15,801 --> 00:32:18,270
and in winter, she catches pheasants
and wild boars.

547
00:32:18,336 --> 00:32:19,638
Is her name Bul-ja?

548
00:32:19,704 --> 00:32:22,073
Don't tell me Bul-ja is short
for illegal immigrant?

549
00:32:22,140 --> 00:32:23,375
-Hey, watch your--
-That's right!

550
00:32:23,442 --> 00:32:24,309
How'd you know?

551
00:32:24,376 --> 00:32:26,278
Bul-ja really is short
for illegal immigrant?

552
00:32:26,344 --> 00:32:28,480
She won't tell me her name.
What can I do?

553
00:32:28,547 --> 00:32:31,683
I can't just call her
"Hey, Illegal Immigrant."

554
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:33,518
Hold on.

555
00:32:33,585 --> 00:32:35,120
You said it was a secret.

556
00:32:35,187 --> 00:32:36,421
Won't that make people suspicious?

557
00:32:36,488 --> 00:32:38,657
That's why I said
it's a secret between us!

558
00:32:38,723 --> 00:32:41,460
You have to take this secret
to your grave,

559
00:32:41,526 --> 00:32:44,095
so keep your mouths shut, got it?

560
00:32:44,162 --> 00:32:45,497
Yes, ma'am.

561
00:32:45,564 --> 00:32:47,199
Oh? It's Bul-ja!

562
00:32:47,265 --> 00:32:49,601
Illegal Immigrant, what are you doing?

563
00:32:52,337 --> 00:32:53,972
Hey, kid.

564
00:32:54,739 --> 00:32:57,509
How did you know
she's an illegal immigrant?

565
00:32:58,610 --> 00:33:01,146
Hey, you brat! I told you
that was our secret!

566
00:33:01,213 --> 00:33:02,781
Take it to your grave!

567
00:33:02,848 --> 00:33:05,617
Ugh, you little blabbermouth.

568
00:33:05,684 --> 00:33:07,819
What good is a loose mouth like yours!

569
00:33:07,886 --> 00:33:09,354
This little brat, seriously.

570
00:33:09,421 --> 00:33:11,690
Not sure who the real blabbermouth is.

571
00:33:11,756 --> 00:33:14,426
Anyway, nobody in this town is normal.

572
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:17,729
Hey, kid, you're Yun-hui's son, right?

573
00:33:17,796 --> 00:33:21,066
Mom told me not to talk to you guys.

574
00:33:24,803 --> 00:33:27,339
What are we, germs? Bacteria?

575
00:33:27,405 --> 00:33:28,874
Wow, this is unbelievable.

576
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:30,475
Unbelievable! Ugh!

577
00:33:31,243 --> 00:33:32,511
Huh? What was that?

578
00:33:33,678 --> 00:33:34,613
What was that?

579
00:33:42,053 --> 00:33:44,789
He did that on purpose, didn't he?
Right?

580
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:51,785
BUS STOP, HADUROK-RI

581
00:33:54,533 --> 00:33:57,602
Looks like the whole town
banded together to drive us out.

582
00:33:57,669 --> 00:34:00,171
Do they really think we'll cave?

583
00:34:00,939 --> 00:34:02,807
From now on, it's war. War!

584
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:03,909
Right.

585
00:34:03,975 --> 00:34:06,411
Too bad the catch is
we have zero weapons.

586
00:34:09,414 --> 00:34:10,782
Jeez, you scared me!

587
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:16,922
Wow, there's no end
to how creepy she is.

588
00:34:18,223 --> 00:34:20,091
Let's hurry up and go. Jeez.

589
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:29,990
VILLAGE BUS, INDIE

590
00:34:36,508 --> 00:34:39,844
Song Hwa-ran, long time no see.
Heading into town?

591
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:42,847
They're cracking down hard
on illegals lately, so be careful.

592
00:34:45,183 --> 00:34:47,586
Song Hwa-ran, come sit right here.

593
00:34:48,353 --> 00:34:50,922
My goodness, you caught so many snakes.

594
00:34:50,989 --> 00:34:53,158
Song Hwa-ran, you're gonna be rich!

595
00:34:53,224 --> 00:34:55,560
Must be hard feeding your family
back in Yanbian.

596
00:34:55,627 --> 00:34:58,029
What? People from other towns
all know, too?

597
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,899
Let's be extra careful
around that lady from now on.

598
00:35:06,404 --> 00:35:08,239
-Oh, my.
-What a nice surprise!

599
00:35:08,306 --> 00:35:11,876
With music playing like this,
it makes me want to dance!

600
00:35:15,647 --> 00:35:17,882
Is this a bus or a marketplace?

601
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:19,584
It's loud as hell.

602
00:35:19,651 --> 00:35:22,420
Why? It has a nice, folksy charm.

603
00:35:22,487 --> 00:35:24,923
Then live here if you like it so much.

604
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:27,926
Can she even see where she's going
like that?

605
00:35:27,993 --> 00:35:30,895
Of course she can.
Why else would she go around like that?

606
00:35:35,533 --> 00:35:37,869
Guess she can't see.

607
00:35:37,936 --> 00:35:42,307
TERMINAL SUPERMARKET

608
00:35:44,075 --> 00:35:45,710
TASTY SUNDAE, HOTTEOK, ODENG

609
00:35:47,846 --> 00:35:49,314
Min-ki, please!

610
00:35:50,382 --> 00:35:53,418
Can't we have just one each?

611
00:35:53,485 --> 00:35:55,220
Yep, no way.

612
00:35:55,286 --> 00:35:56,721
Don't you know we're flat broke?

613
00:35:56,788 --> 00:35:59,257
How much could that tiny thing cost?
Just one each.

614
00:35:59,324 --> 00:36:00,992
I said no.

615
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:03,094
Let's go buy cabbage seeds.

616
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:05,030
-What about this?
-No.

617
00:36:05,096 --> 00:36:06,631
-Just give me one.
-No way.

618
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:13,038
2.5 million won?

619
00:36:13,104 --> 00:36:15,640
Wait, 2.5 million won
just for cabbage seeds?

620
00:36:15,707 --> 00:36:16,641
You said 100,000 heads.

621
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:18,209
You need that much.

622
00:36:18,276 --> 00:36:21,713
Plus, you'll need seedling trays
to plant them in.

623
00:36:21,780 --> 00:36:23,615
For 100,000 heads,
with 50-cell trays,

624
00:36:23,682 --> 00:36:25,817
you'll need at least 2,000 of them.

625
00:36:29,654 --> 00:36:30,755
One million won.

626
00:36:30,822 --> 00:36:34,426
And you'll also need potting soil
for the seedlings.

627
00:36:34,492 --> 00:36:38,096
Add it all up,
and I'll knock off the spare change.

628
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,398
Four million won.

629
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:44,269
Four million won?

630
00:36:47,138 --> 00:36:51,009
Um… Could we pay in installments?

631
00:36:55,346 --> 00:36:58,850
Hey, Hyuk, got any money?
You're rich, you know.

632
00:36:58,917 --> 00:37:01,486
My dad's rich, not me.

633
00:37:01,553 --> 00:37:03,388
I don't have a single dime.

634
00:37:03,455 --> 00:37:07,459
Seriously, you're completely useless.

635
00:37:08,193 --> 00:37:09,994
Pay us! Pay us!

636
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:12,664
Down with the crooked boss! Step down!

637
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:14,265
Step down! Step down!

638
00:37:14,332 --> 00:37:15,500
Huh?

639
00:37:15,567 --> 00:37:19,037
Isn't that the girl
called Bul-ja or whatever?

640
00:37:19,104 --> 00:37:19,971
It is her.

641
00:37:20,038 --> 00:37:23,241
Out of all the money to steal,
he's ripping off their wages?

642
00:37:24,876 --> 00:37:25,977
Poor things.

643
00:37:26,044 --> 00:37:28,613
We're just as pitiful as they are.

644
00:37:29,681 --> 00:37:31,683
Mind your own business
and let's go grocery shopping.

645
00:37:31,750 --> 00:37:32,617
Move along.

646
00:37:32,684 --> 00:37:35,253
Down with the crooked boss! Step down!

647
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:37,288
Step down! Step down!

648
00:37:37,355 --> 00:37:39,891
Hey, Tan! What's wrong with you?

649
00:37:39,958 --> 00:37:42,861
Doing this won't make money
appear out of thin air!

650
00:37:42,927 --> 00:37:45,630
We work harder than Koreans,

651
00:37:45,697 --> 00:37:46,898
and we didn't get paid.

652
00:37:46,965 --> 00:37:50,301
Without that money,
our families will starve.

653
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:51,736
Give us our money.

654
00:37:51,803 --> 00:37:56,674
Today, we won't budge an inch
until you pay us.

655
00:37:59,677 --> 00:38:01,412
Suit yourselves.

656
00:38:01,479 --> 00:38:03,448
Try it forever! See if any money shows up.

657
00:38:03,515 --> 00:38:06,050
PAY OUR BACK WAGES
STOP BLEEDING US DRY

658
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:08,386
BAD BOSS

659
00:38:09,821 --> 00:38:11,156
What do we do now?

660
00:38:11,222 --> 00:38:13,057
Report them as illegal immigrants.

661
00:38:13,124 --> 00:38:14,959
-Is this the place?
-Is it?

662
00:38:15,026 --> 00:38:16,628
Oh, puppies.

663
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:19,664
So cute.

664
00:38:20,865 --> 00:38:23,101
Hey, what are you eating?

665
00:38:27,172 --> 00:38:29,908
Mister, why isn't that one eating?

666
00:38:29,974 --> 00:38:33,411
That weak little thing
won't last much longer.

667
00:38:34,179 --> 00:38:36,881
Still, you should let it eat
with the others.

668
00:38:36,948 --> 00:38:39,884
Why feed a dying dog?
It's just a waste of my money.

669
00:38:43,121 --> 00:38:44,389
What did you just say?

670
00:38:44,455 --> 00:38:47,625
Dog food is way too expensive
these days.

671
00:38:48,793 --> 00:38:53,164
Even so, does a dying dog
not deserve to eat?

672
00:38:53,231 --> 00:38:56,167
Even if it's going to die,
you still have to feed it!

673
00:38:56,234 --> 00:38:57,368
What's wrong, man?

674
00:38:57,435 --> 00:38:59,270
Let go, jeez!

675
00:38:59,337 --> 00:39:02,674
Mister, don't you feel sorry
for this tiny thing?

676
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:04,943
Dying is sad enough as it is.

677
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:07,378
Starving it too is way too cruel!

678
00:39:07,445 --> 00:39:09,247
Knock it off. What's with you?

679
00:39:09,314 --> 00:39:12,984
If you feel so sorry for it,
you buy it.

680
00:39:14,152 --> 00:39:15,620
Stop it, okay?

681
00:39:19,958 --> 00:39:22,660
Hey, can we afford
to raise a dog right now?

682
00:39:22,727 --> 00:39:25,363
We're dead broke!
Why did you buy a dog?

683
00:39:25,430 --> 00:39:26,531
Go return it now.

684
00:39:26,598 --> 00:39:29,033
No! Don't you feel sorry for him?

685
00:39:29,100 --> 00:39:30,635
Whether human or animal,

686
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:32,971
being sick is the saddest thing, man.

687
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:37,208
Hey, we're way more pitiful
than him right now.

688
00:39:37,275 --> 00:39:40,712
Our power was cut off,
and the water's next.

689
00:39:40,778 --> 00:39:44,649
Why do you care if this damn mutt
lives or dies right now?

690
00:39:47,952 --> 00:39:51,689
Hey, do you even know
what it's like to die?

691
00:39:51,756 --> 00:39:53,825
Do you have any idea
how terrifying it is?

692
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:56,861
You heartless bastard!

693
00:39:59,330 --> 00:40:01,032
What's wrong with him lately?

694
00:40:01,099 --> 00:40:03,368
A side effect of first love?

695
00:40:04,002 --> 00:40:06,638
Wait, where did Han Ki-jun go?

696
00:40:09,173 --> 00:40:11,309
Glad I secretly pocketed 1,000 won.

697
00:40:11,376 --> 00:40:12,644
They wouldn't even buy me one,

698
00:40:12,710 --> 00:40:15,813
making me stoop this low.

699
00:40:16,881 --> 00:40:19,651
Guys, I'm sorry…

700
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,686
What's that, jeez?

701
00:40:30,194 --> 00:40:34,265
Seoul or the sticks,
life really is a war everywhere.

702
00:40:40,638 --> 00:40:42,273
Let's hang in there.

703
00:40:58,790 --> 00:41:00,625
No!

704
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:04,062
What the heck did you just do?

705
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:06,831
Pay for my Hotteok!

706
00:41:09,968 --> 00:41:12,470
Please help me.

707
00:41:12,537 --> 00:41:13,805
-What?
-Please help me.

708
00:41:13,871 --> 00:41:16,975
If I'm caught, I'll be deported.
I'm begging you.

709
00:41:17,041 --> 00:41:18,977
-What are you saying?
-Hey, get her!

710
00:41:19,043 --> 00:41:20,778
Get her!

711
00:41:20,845 --> 00:41:22,880
This is driving me crazy.

712
00:41:24,248 --> 00:41:26,284
What? Are you hurt?

713
00:41:27,051 --> 00:41:29,320
Gosh, what do I do?

714
00:41:29,387 --> 00:41:31,689
-Let me see.
-Hold on, stop!

715
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:33,458
Over there!

716
00:41:34,592 --> 00:41:36,060
-Get on.
-How could I…

717
00:41:36,127 --> 00:41:37,462
Get on, quick!

718
00:41:39,230 --> 00:41:41,165
Stop right there! Get them!

719
00:41:41,232 --> 00:41:42,900
Stop right there!

720
00:41:44,302 --> 00:41:46,004
Hey, stop right there!

721
00:41:48,639 --> 00:41:51,342
-Out of the way!
-Hey, stop right there!

722
00:41:51,409 --> 00:41:54,178
-Hey!
-There they go! Stop them!

723
00:41:54,245 --> 00:41:55,680
Whatever, I don't care.

724
00:41:55,747 --> 00:41:57,048
Hey!

725
00:41:58,149 --> 00:41:59,517
Which way?

726
00:41:59,584 --> 00:42:01,819
Where'd the guy go?
There he is!

727
00:42:03,721 --> 00:42:06,024
Why are there so many alleys?

728
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:09,560
Found it! Found the way out!

729
00:42:11,596 --> 00:42:13,965
-Did they go this way?
-Over there!

730
00:42:17,135 --> 00:42:19,737
Ma'am, watch the hot soup!
Out of the way!

731
00:42:20,405 --> 00:42:22,106
I don't know where to go.

732
00:42:27,178 --> 00:42:28,713
They're not following.

733
00:42:32,016 --> 00:42:34,352
They stopped chasing us.

734
00:42:38,256 --> 00:42:39,924
Just a little further.

735
00:42:45,329 --> 00:42:47,799
What do you think you're doing?

736
00:42:47,865 --> 00:42:49,667
I'm so sorry.

737
00:42:50,334 --> 00:42:52,503
-Wait.
-There they are! Freeze!

738
00:42:53,704 --> 00:42:55,440
What are you doing? Run!

739
00:42:55,506 --> 00:42:57,575
You'll get caught. Go, quick!

740
00:42:59,277 --> 00:43:00,144
Go!

741
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:02,246
Go! Hurry, run!

742
00:43:04,015 --> 00:43:06,284
Go!

743
00:43:08,986 --> 00:43:10,321
Go!

744
00:43:18,830 --> 00:43:20,465
-Why are you doing this?
-Hold still!

745
00:43:20,531 --> 00:43:21,866
What did I do? Let go!

746
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,235
You're under arrest for illegal stay.

747
00:43:24,302 --> 00:43:26,404
[speaking foreign language]

748
00:43:26,471 --> 00:43:31,142
[speaking foreign language]

749
00:43:31,209 --> 00:43:33,277
[speaking foreign language]

750
00:43:33,344 --> 00:43:35,580
Now, now, quiet down!

751
00:43:35,646 --> 00:43:37,815
These people are driving me crazy!

752
00:43:37,882 --> 00:43:39,884
UNITE AND FIGHT

753
00:43:39,951 --> 00:43:42,720
speaking foreign language

754
00:43:45,356 --> 00:43:46,824
speaking foreign language

755
00:43:47,758 --> 00:43:50,761
speaking foreign language

756
00:43:50,828 --> 00:43:52,997
-What?
-speaking foreign language

757
00:43:53,531 --> 00:43:55,766
I'm Korean! Me!

758
00:43:55,833 --> 00:43:57,468
I don't speak your language!

759
00:43:57,535 --> 00:43:58,970
Why keep talking to me?

760
00:43:59,036 --> 00:44:00,805
I'm already pissed off as it is.

761
00:44:06,344 --> 00:44:08,880
Officer, you're making
a huge mistake right now.

762
00:44:08,946 --> 00:44:12,950
I really am Korean!
Born and raised in Ssangmun-dong, Seoul!

763
00:44:14,619 --> 00:44:16,254
We'll find out soon, punk.

764
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,455
Wait your turn.

765
00:44:17,522 --> 00:44:19,624
I'm going crazy, jeez.

766
00:44:20,658 --> 00:44:22,360
Wait!

767
00:44:22,426 --> 00:44:25,863
I can just show you my ID card, right?

768
00:44:25,930 --> 00:44:28,666
How many times did I tell you
I'm Korean?

769
00:44:28,733 --> 00:44:30,001
Here, look! Look!

770
00:44:30,067 --> 00:44:31,636
HAN KI-JUN
901025-1041118

771
00:44:47,785 --> 00:44:48,653
Why hit me?

772
